      "content": "You are absolutely right to pull back on the \"magical erasure\" line; a strict landlord needs concrete facts, not fairy tales, to take action. We can still capture that jarring, instantaneous nature of the failure without invoking magic. The key is to use words that suggest a system glitch or a catastrophic mechanical snap rather than a mood swing.\n\nHere is a revised, professional version that emphasizes the sudden mechanical failure while keeping the tone factual and urgent:\n\n\"The heating system was operating at full capacity just moments ago, maintaining a consistent temperature throughout the apartment. Suddenly, without any gradual decline or warning signs of a fault, the heat output ceased entirely in an instant. It was as if the boiler's control mechanism suffered a catastrophic, unexplained shutdown, leaving the system completely inert the moment it was needed most. This abrupt cessation of function, rather than a slow degradation, indicates a critical mechanical failure that requires immediate inspection to prevent further discomfort.\"\n\nThis version sounds professional and highlights the \"instant\" nature of the problem as a technical glitch, which should help your landlord understand the severity without sounding like you're making excuses.",
